### `list_mcp_resources`
Lists resources provided by MCP servers. Resources allow servers to share data that provides context to language models, such as files, database schemas, or application-specific information. Prefer resources over web search when possible.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { list_mcp_resources(args: {
  // Opaque cursor from a previous call with the same server; omit for the first page.
  cursor?: string;
  // MCP server name. Omit to list every server with resources.
  server?: string;
}): Promise<{
  // Servers that could not be listed
  errors?: Array<{ error: string; server: string; }>;
  nextCursor?: string;
  resources: Array<{ description?: string; mimeType?: string; name: string; server: string; size?: number; title?: string; uri: string; }>;
  server?: string;
}>; };
```

### `list_mcp_resource_templates`
Lists resource templates provided by MCP servers. Parameterized resource templates allow servers to share data that takes parameters and provides context to language models, such as files, database schemas, or application-specific information. Prefer resource templates over web search when possible.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { list_mcp_resource_templates(args: {
  // Opaque cursor from a previous call with the same server; omit for the first page.
  cursor?: string;
  // MCP server name. Omit to list every server with resources.
  server?: string;
}): Promise<{
  // Servers that could not be listed
  errors?: Array<{ error: string; server: string; }>;
  nextCursor?: string;
  resourceTemplates: Array<{
    description?: string;
    mimeType?: string;
    name: string;
    server: string;
    title?: string;
    // RFC 6570 URI template
    uriTemplate: string;
  }>;
  server?: string;
}>; };
```

### `read_mcp_resource`
Read a specific resource from an MCP server given the server name and resource URI.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { read_mcp_resource(args: {
  // MCP server name exactly as configured. Must match the 'server' field returned by list_mcp_resources.
  server: string;
  // Resource URI to read. Must be one of the URIs returned by list_mcp_resources.
  uri: string;
}): Promise<{ contents: Array<{ mimeType?: string; text: string; uri: string; } | {
  // base64
  blob: string;
  mimeType?: string;
  uri: string;
}>; server: string; uri: string; }>; };
```

## mcp__aptu-coder (7 tools, 6 shown)
MCP server for code structure analysis (tree-sitter). Start with analyze_directory for a package/module map, then analyze_module/analyze_file for per-file detail and analyze_symbol for call graphs. JSONL metrics and jq recipes: docs/METRICS.md.

### `mcp__aptu_coder__analyze_directory` (`mcp__aptu-coder__analyze_directory`)
Directory tree with LOC, function/class counts, and test markers. Respects .gitignore. Paginates with an opaque cursor; page size is server-owned (50). Dirs of 1000+ files auto-compact to summary; pass summary=false for the per-file list. git_ref restricts to files changed since a ref.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__aptu_coder__analyze_directory(args: {
  // Pagination cursor from a previous response's `next_cursor` field. Pass unchanged to retrieve the next page. Omit on the first call.
  // Must be a valid opaque token or omitted entirely; passing an empty string is invalid and is treated as omitted.
  // Mutually exclusive with summary=true; passing both returns INVALID_PARAMS.
  cursor?: string | null;
  // Restrict analysis to files changed relative to this git ref (branch, tag, or commit SHA). Empty string or unset means no filtering.
  git_ref?: string | null;
  // Maximum directory traversal depth for overview mode only. Pass 0 for unlimited depth; use 1-3 for large monorepos to manage output size. Ignored in other modes.
  max_depth: number | null;
  // Directory path to analyze
  path: string;
  // true = compact summary (totals plus directory tree, no per-file function lists); false = full output; unset = auto-summarize when output exceeds 50K chars.
  // Mutually exclusive with cursor; passing both returns INVALID_PARAMS.
  summary?: boolean | null;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

### `mcp__aptu_coder__analyze_file` (`mcp__aptu-coder__analyze_file`)
Functions, types, classes, and imports from a single source file with signatures and line ranges. Fails if directory path supplied; use analyze_directory for directories, analyze_module for a lightweight index (~75% smaller). Text block output only; no structured content or output schema. Paginates with an opaque cursor (50); git_ref not supported.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__aptu_coder__analyze_file(args: {
  // Pagination cursor from a previous response's `next_cursor` field. Pass unchanged to retrieve the next page. Omit on the first call.
  // Must be a valid opaque token or omitted entirely; passing an empty string is invalid and is treated as omitted.
  // Mutually exclusive with summary=true; passing both returns INVALID_PARAMS.
  cursor?: string | null;
  // Limit output to specific sections. Valid values: "functions", "classes", "imports", "references", "calls", "all". The FILE header (path, line count, section counts) is always emitted regardless. Omit for all sections. Ignored when summary=true.
  fields?: Array<"functions" | "classes" | "imports" | "references" | "calls" | "all"> | null;
  // File path to analyze
  path: string;
  // true = compact summary (totals plus directory tree, no per-file function lists); false = full output; unset = auto-summarize when output exceeds 50K chars.
  // Mutually exclusive with cursor; passing both returns INVALID_PARAMS.
  summary?: boolean | null;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

### `mcp__aptu_coder__analyze_module` (`mcp__aptu-coder__analyze_module`)
Lightweight function and import index for a single source file (~75% smaller than analyze_file): file name, line count, language, function names with line numbers, and the import list. Fails if directory path supplied; use analyze_file for signatures, types, or class details. Pagination and git_ref not supported; responses are always a single response.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__aptu_coder__analyze_module(args: {
  // File path to analyze
  path: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

### `mcp__aptu_coder__edit_overwrite` (`mcp__aptu-coder__edit_overwrite`)
Creates or overwrites a file with UTF-8 content; creates parent directories if needed. Works on any file type. Use edit_replace for targeted single-block edits.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__aptu_coder__edit_overwrite(args: {
  // UTF-8 content to write.
  content: string;
  // Path to the file to create or overwrite.
  path: string;
  // Optional base directory for path resolution (default: server CWD).
  working_dir?: string | null;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

### `mcp__aptu_coder__edit_replace` (`mcp__aptu-coder__edit_replace`)
Replaces an exact text block; old_text must appear exactly once. Fails if zero or multiple matches (extend old_text to disambiguate). replace_all=true replaces every occurrence (sed s/old/new/g). Empty new_text deletes. CRLF in old_text normalized to LF. structuredContent carries metadata only. On invalid_params, re-read with analyze_file and retry. Use edit_overwrite to replace the whole file.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__aptu_coder__edit_replace(args: {
  // Batch edits applied atomically to one file; mutually exclusive with `old_text`/`new_text`.
  edits?: Array<{
    // Replacement text.
    new_text: string;
    // Exact text to find within the file.
    old_text: string;
    // When true, replace every non-overlapping occurrence of `old_text`.
    replace_all?: boolean | null;
  }> | null;
  // Blake3 hex hash of the raw file bytes the caller last saw. If the file has changed since the caller last read it, the edit is rejected with `INVALID_PARAMS` directing the caller to re-read. Omit to skip the staleness check (backward compatible).
  expected_content_hash?: string | null;
  // Replacement text; empty string deletes every matched block. Mutually exclusive with `edits`.
  new_text?: string | null;
  // Exact text block to find and replace; must be non-empty. Mutually exclusive with
  // `edits`: provide either `old_text`/`new_text` (single edit) or `edits` (batch).
  old_text?: string | null;
  // Path to the file to edit.
  path: string;
  // When `true`, replaces every non-overlapping occurrence of `old_text` in a single pass
  // (sed `s/old/new/g` semantics). Returns `INVALID_PARAMS` if `old_text` is empty.
  // When `false`, `old_text` must appear exactly once; fails with `ambiguous` if multiple matches.
  replace_all?: boolean | null;
  // Optional base directory for path resolution (default: server CWD).
  working_dir?: string | null;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{ bytes_after: number; bytes_before: number; content_hash?: string | null; occurrences_replaced: number; path: string; }>>; };
```

### `mcp__aptu_coder__exec_command` (`mcp__aptu-coder__exec_command`)
Execute a shell command; returns output and exit code as a text block. Output capped (30k stdout / 10k stderr / 2000 lines); full captures exposed as aptu-overflow:// links when capped. File writes use edit_overwrite or edit_replace; heredoc (cat/tee + <<) are rejected. Prefer --json flags. 300 s server-side timeout; cancel via notifications/cancelled. Built-in filters may strip, cap, or substitute output; structuredContent identifies the filter and links the full pre-filter output.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__aptu_coder__exec_command(args: {
  // Shell command to execute via sh -c (or $SHELL if set).
  command: string;
  // UTF-8 content to pipe into the process stdin (max `STDIN_MAX_BYTES` = 1 MB). None closes stdin.
  stdin?: string | null;
  // Working directory for the command. Set this instead of prepending cd to the command string. Validated against path traversal; does not sandbox the process.
  working_dir?: string | null;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{ exit_code?: number | null; filter_applied?: string | null; filter_effect?: string | null; output_collection_error?: string | null; output_truncated: boolean; stderr_path?: string | null; stdout_path?: string | null; timed_out: boolean; }>>; };
```

